---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Binary } from '@lucide/astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Nintendo Entertainment System – Learn 6502 Assembly Through Games"
  description="Learn NES 6502 assembly by building complete games. Master the PPU, APU, and the processor that powered the console revolution."
>
  <style>
    .system-hero {
      min-height: 350px;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #e30613 0%, #ff4444 100%);
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .system-hero::before {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      right: 0;
      bottom: 0;
      background-image:
        repeating-linear-gradient(
          45deg,
          transparent,
          transparent 10px,
          rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1) 10px,
          rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1) 20px
        );
      pointer-events: none;
    }

    .hero-content {
      text-align: center;
      color: white;
      padding: var(--space-8) var(--space-4);
      position: relative;
      z-index: 1;
      max-width: 800px;
    }

    .system-title {
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
      font-weight: 900;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
      text-shadow: 3px 3px 0px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    }

    .system-subtitle {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      opacity: 0.95;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    }

    .system-specs {
      display: flex;
      gap: var(--space-6);
      justify-content: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      margin-top: var(--space-4);
    }

    .spec-item {
      text-align: center;
    }

    .spec-label {
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      opacity: 0.8;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    }

    .spec-value {
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: 1rem;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    .content-section {
      padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-4);
      max-width: 1000px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .section-title {
      font-size: 1.75rem;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
      color: var(--color-text);
      text-align: center;
    }

    .section-intro {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
      max-width: 700px;
      text-align: center;
      margin-left: auto;
      margin-right: auto;
    }

    /* Single Path Card */
    .path-container {
      max-width: 500px;
      margin: var(--space-8) auto 0;
    }

    .path-card {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 2px solid #e30613;
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: var(--space-8);
      text-decoration: none;
      color: var(--color-text);
      transition: all var(--transition-base);
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .path-card:hover {
      transform: translateY(-4px);
      box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgba(227, 6, 19, 0.2);
    }

    .path-title {
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: 1.75rem;
      font-weight: 900;
      color: #e30613;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    }

    .path-subtitle {
      font-size: 1rem;
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    }

    .path-description {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    }

    .path-stats {
      display: flex;
      gap: var(--space-6);
      padding-top: var(--space-4);
      border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    }

    .path-stat {
      text-align: center;
    }

    .stat-value {
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: 1.5rem;
      font-weight: 900;
      color: #e30613;
    }

    .stat-label {
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .path-icon {
      color: #e30613;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    }

    .path-cta {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-6);
      background: #e30613;
      color: white;
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      text-decoration: none;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-top: var(--space-4);
      text-align: center;
    }

    .console-note {
      text-align: center;
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      margin-top: var(--space-8);
      padding: var(--space-4);
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    }

    /* Vault Section */
    .vault-section {
      padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-4);
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    }

    .vault-container {
      max-width: 1000px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .vault-header {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    }

    .vault-title {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .vault-link {
      color: #e30613;
      text-decoration: none;
      font-weight: 500;
    }

    .vault-link:hover {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .vault-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(280px, 1fr));
      gap: var(--space-4);
    }

    .vault-card {
      display: block;
      padding: var(--space-6);
      background: var(--color-bg);
      border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      text-decoration: none;
      color: var(--color-text);
      transition: all var(--transition-base);
    }

    .vault-card:hover {
      border-color: #e30613;
      transform: translateY(-2px);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
    }

    .vault-kicker {
      display: block;
      font-size: 0.7rem;
      color: #e30613;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
    }

    .vault-name {
      display: block;
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    }

    .vault-desc {
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    /* About Section */
    .about-section {
      padding: var(--space-10) var(--space-4);
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .about-title {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .about-text {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .about-text p {
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    }

    .about-text p:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .system-specs {
        gap: var(--space-4);
      }

      .vault-header {
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: flex-start;
        gap: var(--space-2);
      }
    }
  </style>

  <!-- System Hero -->
  <section class="system-hero">
    <div class="hero-content">
      <h1 class="system-title">NINTENDO ENTERTAINMENT SYSTEM</h1>
      <p class="system-subtitle">Learn 6502 assembly by building games</p>
      <div class="system-specs">
        <div class="spec-item">
          <div class="spec-label">CPU</div>
          <div class="spec-value">Ricoh 2A03</div>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-item">
          <div class="spec-label">Speed</div>
          <div class="spec-value">1.79 MHz</div>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-item">
          <div class="spec-label">RAM</div>
          <div class="spec-value">2 KB</div>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-item">
          <div class="spec-label">Graphics</div>
          <div class="spec-value">PPU</div>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-item">
          <div class="spec-label">Sound</div>
          <div class="spec-value">APU</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- About This System -->
  <section class="about-section">
    <h2 class="about-title">Why the Nintendo Entertainment System?</h2>
    <div class="about-text">
      <p>
        The NES didn't just revive the video game industry after the crash of 1983 — it defined what console gaming could be. Nintendo's strict quality control created a library of legendary titles: Super Mario Bros, The Legend of Zelda, Metroid, Mega Man. These weren't just fun games; they were masterclasses in design and programming efficiency.
      </p>
      <p>
        With just 2 KB of RAM and a 1.79 MHz processor, NES developers achieved remarkable things through clever use of the PPU (Picture Processing Unit) and APU (Audio Processing Unit). Learning NES development teaches you to think in tiles and sprites, to squeeze every cycle from limited hardware, and to understand the console architecture that shaped an entire industry. The homebrew community remains active, with new games still being released on original cartridges.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Single Path -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">The Assembly Path</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">
      The NES has no built-in programming language — everything is assembly. Master the PPU, APU, and the 6502 processor that powered the console revolution.
    </p>

    <div class="path-container">
      <a href="/nintendo-entertainment-system/assembly" class="path-card">
        <div class="path-icon"><Binary size={32} /></div>
        <h3 class="path-title">6502 Assembly</h3>
        <p class="path-subtitle">Full hardware control</p>
        <p class="path-description">
          Learn the architecture behind Super Mario Bros, The Legend of Zelda, and Mega Man. Master the PPU for tiles and sprites, the APU for iconic 8-bit sound, and cartridge mappers for games that pushed beyond the hardware limits.
        </p>
        <div class="path-stats">
          <div class="path-stat">
            <div class="stat-value">18</div>
            <div class="stat-label">Games</div>
          </div>
          <div class="path-stat">
            <div class="stat-value">1,408</div>
            <div class="stat-label">Units</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <span class="path-cta">Start Building Games</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="console-note">
      Unlike home computers of the era, the NES was a dedicated games console with no built-in BASIC. All NES development is in assembly — and that's what made it special.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Vault Section -->
  <section class="vault-section">
    <div class="vault-container">
      <div class="vault-header">
        <h2 class="vault-title">From the Vault</h2>
        <a href="/vault" class="vault-link">View all articles</a>
      </div>
      <div class="vault-grid">
        <a href="/vault/systems/nes" class="vault-card">
          <span class="vault-kicker">Hardware</span>
          <span class="vault-name">Nintendo Entertainment System</span>
          <span class="vault-desc">The 8-bit console that revived home gaming and defined a generation of players.</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/vault/culture/bedroom-coder" class="vault-card">
          <span class="vault-kicker">Culture</span>
          <span class="vault-name">The Bedroom Coder</span>
          <span class="vault-desc">How teenagers with cassette decks built a multi-billion pound industry.</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/vault/techniques/cassette-loading" class="vault-card">
          <span class="vault-kicker">Technique</span>
          <span class="vault-name">Cassette Loading</span>
          <span class="vault-desc">How magnetic tape became playable games - the technology behind the loading screen.</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
